This licence is written in plain language on purpose. It is short because the
permission being granted is narrow.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 1. WHAT YOU MAY DO
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

 a) Use PIP-MON, and anything built from it, for your own personal use.

 b) Run it alongside your own mods, on your own machine, for your own play.

 c) Read the source code, in full, for any purpose.

 d) Modify the source code for your own personal use, including changing it so
    it works better on your system, your load order, or your hardware.

 e) Share the COMPILED program with other people for their personal,
    non-commercial use. "Compiled program" means the built binary and its
    required data files -- not the source code, and not the build scripts.

 f) Contribute changes back to the project.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 2. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

 a) You may not publish, post, or otherwise make the SOURCE CODE publicly
    available -- on GitHub, GitLab, a mod page, a Discord server, a paste site,
    a zip you attach to a mod release, or anywhere else others can obtain it.

 b) You may not redistribute the source code, modified or unmodified, including
    as part of a mod, a collection, a tutorial, or a "here's my fork" package.

 c) You may not sell, licence, rent, or otherwise receive payment for PIP-MON
    or anything derived from it, in source or compiled form.

 d) You may not use PIP-MON, or anything derived from it, for commercial
    purposes. That includes monetised mods, paid tiers, advertising-supported
    distributions, and Patreon-style subscriptions that grant access to it.

 e) You may not remove or obscure the copyright notices, this licence, or the
    author's name from any copy you distribute.

 f) You may not present yourself, or any third party, as the author or
    originator of PIP-MON. You may say you modified it; you may not say you
    made it.

 g) You may not use the names "PIP-MON" or "V-Probe" for your own product or
    distribution in a way that suggests it is this project.

